    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Assumptions\n\n- Generic **Webhook** POST `telegram` (not Telegram Trigger); body includes `message.text`.\n- **chatId** resolution order: `message.chat.id`, then `message.chat_id`, then top-level `chat_id`, then **$env.TELEGRAM_REPLY_CHAT_ID** (for minimal test payloads).\n- Ticket test example: `{\"message\":{\"text\":\"Hello, AI!\"}}` works when **TELEGRAM_REPLY_CHAT_ID** is set on the n8n host; or use `{\"message\":{\"text\":\"Hello, AI!\",\"chat\":{\"id\":123}}}`.\n- Inbound auth uses **HTTP Header Auth** credential named **Telegram API**; outbound Telegram uses **telegramApi** with the same display name.\n- OpenAI reply text: `message.content`, else `choices[0].message.content`, else `text`.\n- OpenAI: **gpt-4o-mini**, user message only, maxTokens 500, temperature 0.7; 3 retries with 1s wait between tries.\n- Failures route via **onError → Execute Workflow** id `tg-ai-chatbot-error` (Error Handling workflow)."
      },
      "id": "f2a3b4c5-6d7e-8f9a-3b4c-5d6e7f8091a2",
      "name": "Assumptions",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -200
      ]
    }
